Subject: dptf_enabler: bounds-check GNVS offsets before writing

SET_FLAGS() indexed the remapped GNVS region with hardcoded offsets (up to
0x969 by default, 0xB56 with enable_fans/enable_sensors) without ever
checking them against gnvs_len parsed from the DSDT. memremap(MEMREMAP_WB)
resolves to the cached linear map on x86, so an access past the end does not
fault -- it silently reads and writes adjacent physical memory. The module is
loaded on every boot via /etc/modules-load.d, so a mismatch would repeat.

Measured on this unit: GNVS is at 0x73520000, length 3348 (0xD14), so every
offset is in range today. This guard is for BIOS updates and other units.

--- a/modules/dptf_enabler/dptf_enabler.c
+++ b/modules/dptf_enabler/dptf_enabler.c
@@ -138,7 +138,13 @@
 
 	#define SET_FLAGS(arr) do { \
 		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(arr); i++) { \
-			u8 *p = (u8 *)gnvs + arr[i].off; \
+			u8 *p; \
+			if (arr[i].off >= gnvs_len) { \
+				pr_warn("skip %s: offset 0x%x outside GNVS (len 0x%x)\n", \
+					arr[i].name, arr[i].off, gnvs_len); \
+				continue; \
+			} \
+			p = (u8 *)gnvs + arr[i].off; \
 			if (!*p) { \
 				*p = 1; \
 				n++; \
